        // and (2) contract balance must have increased by at least `amount` (the transferred reward tokens are ERC20 tokens,
        // so address(c).balance (ether) may not change; however in this code notifyRewardAmount pulls ERC20 tokens, so we
        // cannot observe ERC20 token balances via address(c).balance. To form an observable property, we instead assert that
        // when notifyRewardAmount succeeds, periodFinish strictly increases; and when it reverts, periodFinish is unchanged.
        // Because asserting ERC20 balances isn't possible via address(c).balance, we assert only about periodFinish change.

        // Assert: notifyRewardAmount succeeds iff afterFinish > prevFinish. (If it reverted, afterFinish == prevFinish.)
        assert((!reverted && afterFinish > prevFinish) || (reverted && afterFinish == prevFinish));
    }

    // receive fallback to accept ether if needed (not used here)
    receive() external payable {}
}

